course: dictionary
lesson: 4287
title: Greenish and the little -ish
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Greenish is made of two parts: green and -ish. The ending -ish means "a little bit" or "close to", so greenish means a little bit green, or a colour close to green. Bluish is a little bit blue, and reddish is a little bit red.
explain: «Its fur is even a little garden: tiny green algae grow in it and moths live in it, so a still, greenish sloth is hard to spot among the leaves.» The sloth is not bright green. Its fur is a colour close to green, which helps it blend in with the leaves. Ask yourself: what does the -ish change?
explain: Greenish can also describe a face. A character who turns greenish on a boat looks pale and unwell, as if about to be sick. The clues are the boat and the words around it, not just the colour.
fact: Greenish means a little bit green, or a colour close to green.
fact: The ending -ish softens a colour word: greenish, bluish, reddish.
fact: Greenish can describe a pale, ill face, as if about to be sick.
fact: «Blueberries» turn greenish in batter with too much baking soda, and a little lemon juice brings the purple back.
fact: Deer cannot see red and orange well, so an orange tiger looks greenish to them, like grass.
exercise: «Its fur is even a little garden: tiny green algae grow in it, so a still, greenish sloth is hard to spot among the leaves.» What does greenish mean here? | Covered in water | *A little bit green, close to the colour of the leaves | Very old and dusty | Bright red and loud
exercise: Dan says a child who turns greenish on a boat is just happy. What does greenish suggest? | *The child looks pale and may be about to be sick | The child has won a prize | The child is very hot | The child is dancing
exercise: In bluish, reddish and greenish, what does the ending -ish add? | A loud sound | Another word for the colour | A question mark | *A little bit of the colour
test: What colour is a live lobster usually? | Bright red | Pure white | *Dark greenish brown or bluish | Bright yellow
test: Why does an orange tiger look greenish to a deer? | *Deer cannot see red and orange well | The tiger is hiding under water | Deer can only see in black and white | Tigers are always painted green
exam: What can an over-boiled egg get around the yolk? | Pink spots | *A greenish ring | Blue shell | A crack down the middle
